# Cases for the inline answer options reference (#189).
//
// ⭐⭐ NOT ONE SYSTEM URL APPEARS IN THIS FILE. A coded fact on a concept with inline `value from:` options
// carries a BARE option code, and its system is resolved from the `defined by` concept's own answer
// CodeSystem. That is the half of the construct a `.crl`-only fixture cannot prove.
//
// ⚠ THE PAUSE ROWS ARE DELIBERATELY ABSENT, and that is not an omission. `result is` must name a branch, so
// a case whose correct answer is that NO branch fires cannot be written — asserting one would author the
// exact collapse the three-state model exists to prevent. Those rows are proved by `$apply`, not here.
library "CodedQuestionCases".
covers "Coded Question Reference".

fact "Pat":
- name is "Pat".
- birth date is "1970-01-01".
- defined by "Patient".

fact "Requested":
- value is true.
- date is "2026-01-02".
- defined by "Service Requested".

// ⭐ A BARE option code — no system.
fact "Qualifying Symptom":
- value is "functional-limitation".
- date is "2026-01-02".
- defined by "Coded Question Reference"."Documented Symptom".

// ⭐⭐ ONE ANSWER DENIES. Without this option the criterion would stay UNKNOWN and the tree would PAUSE; the
// user would have to answer every symptom NO to reach a denial.
fact "No Listed Symptom":
- value is "none-of-listed".
- date is "2026-01-02".
- defined by "Coded Question Reference"."Documented Symptom".

// ⚠ A code from ANOTHER system. This is why the explicit `<system>|<code>` form stays legal: a bare code
// resolves against the declared options, so it can only ever name a member or a declared non-member.
// Stating a code the question never offered REQUIRES naming its system.
fact "Unoffered Symptom":
- value is "http://example.org/other|functional-limitation".
- date is "2026-01-02".
- defined by "Coded Question Reference"."Documented Symptom".

// ⭐ A LATER answer overrides an earlier one — `most recent this` publishes the newest record.
fact "No Listed Symptom Later":
- value is "none-of-listed".
- date is "2026-03-01".
- defined by "Coded Question Reference"."Documented Symptom".

case "a qualifying answer -> certify":
- subject is "Pat".
- fact is "Requested".
- fact is "Qualifying Symptom".
- result is "Coverage Determination" is "certify.Met".

case "none of the listed -> not certify, in ONE answer":
- subject is "Pat".
- fact is "Requested".
- fact is "No Listed Symptom".
- result is "Coverage Determination" is "not-certify.Unmet".

case "a code from another system is a determinate non-member -> not certify":
- subject is "Pat".
- fact is "Requested".
- fact is "Unoffered Symptom".
- result is "Coverage Determination" is "not-certify.Unmet".

case "a later none answer overrides an earlier qualifying one -> not certify":
- subject is "Pat".
- fact is "Requested".
- fact is "Qualifying Symptom".
- fact is "No Listed Symptom Later".
- result is "Coverage Determination" is "not-certify.Unmet".
